---
description: Rules for v2 version of the code and API development
alwaysApply: true
---
- These rules apply only to work on the v2 version of the code and API.
- The file v2-schema.dat (DBML format) is a reference for what the sqlite v2 database should be
- The development plan is in the file v2-api-implementation-editable.plan.md
- If you come across the word "STOP" in the plan, stop work and wait for user feedback
- All v2 database columns use snake_case
- All API fields use camelCase. API camelCase fields correspond directly to database snake_case fields.  Example:  orgUid -> org_uid, metaKey -> meta_key
- When testing, stop/kill processes when finished. Use `ps aux | grep "src/server.js"` to identify cadt processes and then `kill <PID1 <PID2>` etc to kill the process IDs. Can also use `lsof -ti:31310 | xargs kill -9` to kill the process using the CADT port.  After killing processes, verify they're gone: `ps aux | grep "src/server.js"`
- CHIA_ROOT directory is ~/.chia/mainnet/ and directory for cadt config and database for v2 will be ~/.chia/mainnet/cadt/v2/

# Primary Keys (CRITICAL - Must Follow Exactly)
- Data tables: UUID v4 (varchar(36)) - Generated by application code, NOT database auto-increment
- System tables: INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT
- NEVER use INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT for data tables
- Data table primary keys must be VARCHAR(36) to store UUID strings
- UUIDs are generated in application code using uuid.v4() before database insert

# Foreign Keys
- Application-level validation (no DB constraints)
- Check both main table AND staging table for references
- Enables staging multiple related records before commit

# Timestamps
- Automatically managed by Sequelize (`created_at`, `updated_at`)
- Rejected if provided in POST/PUT requests

# API Request Patterns (CRITICAL - Follows V1)
- Update Requests: MUST include ALL fields, not just the ones being updated
- Create Requests: Include all required fields
- Validation: Same validation schema used for both CREATE and UPDATE operations

# Migration Patterns (CRITICAL)
- Data table migrations: PRIMARY KEY must be VARCHAR(36), NOT INTEGER AUTOINCREMENT
- Data table migrations: Primary key field should be allowNull: false, unique: true
- Data table migrations: NO autoIncrement: true for data tables
- Example: cad_trust_project_id: { type: Sequelize.STRING(36), primaryKey: true, allowNull: false, unique: true }

# Testing
- Always run v2 tests individually to avoid v1 test interference
- Work iteratively and write and run tests when any API endpoint is created or modified.  Additionally, any time significant functionality is added, tests should be created and run as part of the development process.  Create the tests as close to the creation of the functionality as possible - don't wait until a later phase of the project to write the tests.  After running tests and fixing any issues identified by the tests, stop and ask for user input and feedback before proceeding.
- Most tests should use simulation mode, which does not require datalayer or chia to be running. If running a test in simulation mode results in an error with the datalayer connection, something is wrong which needs to be addressed.

# Documentation
- We will write documentation in a specific task, not as we go.
- Documentation should closely follow the formatting, style, and structure of existing v1 documentation at /docs/cadt_rpc_api.md.  v2 documentation should be in file /docs/cadt_rpc_api_v2.md.
